    "title": "Landmark24 Homes named Builder of the Year - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ben Senger ,\n2 hours ago\nSAVANNAH, Ga. (WSAV) — After another sellout campaign, the builder of the Savannah-area St. Jude Dream Home has been named Builder of the Year.\nLandmark24 Homes received the honor at the St. Jude Dream Home Giveaway Builder Summit, held in Memphis in August.\nLandmark24 has built three homes in the area for St. Jude, all of them at zero cost to the hospital.\nThis is the builder’s third award from the Dream Home program. Previously, Landmark24 earned Best First-Year Builder and Best Media and Marketing Integration awards.\nThe 2025 St. Jude Dream Home in Pooler raised $800,000.\nSt. Jude Dream Homes are built in 45 cities around the country each year. More details about the 2026 St. Jude Dream Home will be released in January.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WSAV-TV.",
